Each glyph from a seeded random offset/rotation to rest with easeOutBack plus per-frame motion blur: ±300 px, ±25°, stagger 40 ms, 500 ms (pm-leonkohli-6dc01b); ±60° tumble, stagger 30–40, then stacked offset shadows 4 px & 8 px in two accents (pm-ik-builds-b8bdcf); rotateZ/Y −40° + drop shadow, stagger 70 (pm-sudo-kiran-49176d); gravity drop 30–60 px, ±25°, stagger 40, contrasted with a calm italic serif word (pm-levabashidze-2d713a); signature letters fall 500 ms bounce-lite with irregular 60–120 ms stagger onto a visible grid baseline (pm-fionntobin-97b7af); a letter falls onto notebook rules (pm-lexnlin-038035). Vortex variant: each glyph on a polar spiral (r, θ) around its target, animate r → 0 and θ → 0 with rotation and motion blur, stagger 30 ms, ~700 ms ease-out (pm-1littlecoder-9fef89). Ready-made char-slam-explode: seeded scatter hold → overshooting slam + 3-frame landing shake (spread tight|wild). | code (js): const r = MOTION.rng(7);                         // seeded: identical every render
letters.forEach((el, i) => tl.from(el, {
  x: (r() * 2 - 1) * 300, y: (r() * 2 - 1) * 300, rotation: (r() * 2 - 1) * 25,
  opacity: 0, duration: 0.5, ease: "back.out(1.6)" }, at + i * 0.04));

Sparse array of {t, text}; onUpdate reverse-searches the latest passed state (no interpolation) → typos, holds, bulk pastes and backspaces; first keystrokes 3–5 characters 0.1–0.2 s apart; driver ease none. Context caret: its background colour switches at segment boundaries; blink = (tl.time() % cycle) < cycle / 2; 4–8 s per typed line. Caret Swap: a gradient caret #FF4DAA → #8A5CF6 spreads over a phrase, collapses left, then types the replacement (font_size 72, 36–160; weight 400–700; Geist bundled). Terminal-then-display: 40 ms/char, caret blink 500 ms, then a 250 ms scale snap to a 160 px display face — not a crossfade (brief pm-danilowm-d3720d). Typewriter-reveal blueprint (3.6–7 s): the caret types and edits like a human, then collapses into the brand payoff or types a CTA rail under a standing logo; icon slides left, name typed, tagline fades (pm-tdinh-me-815acb). | code (js): const STATES = [{t: 0, text: ""}, {t: .12, text: "Shp"}, {t: .45, text: "Sh"},
  {t: .6, text: "Ship it"}, {t: 1.3, text: "Ship it today."}];          // typo → backspace → fix
const textAt = (s) => STATES.reduce((cur, st) => (st.t <= s ? st : cur), STATES[0]).text;
tl.to({}, { duration: 2, onUpdate() { el.textContent = textAt(this.time()); } }, at);

beatsFor(tokens): n = min(5, max(3, ceil(words / 6))) beats per clip; ≤6 words per beat, ≤30 words per clip (hard error beyond); hero = first word with 3–10 alphanumerics, lead = words before it, tail = words after; beat j owns [j·len/n, (j+1)·len/n] s and is fully cleared before the next; small type = ¼ of the headline height; pace 2.5 words/s fast, 1.8 relaxed; timestamped scripts (‘0–3s: …’) must be ordered and non-overlapping. Part of the kinetic-flow profile (17 themes A–Q, 8/10 s clips, 9:16 / 16:9 / 1:1), which emits Google Flow prompts — the beat grid itself is engine-agnostic: render it with TYPE-14 + TYPE-41. Proven: node --test tests/production-profiles.test.mjs → 10/10 pass in this container. Gap: hero detection uses [a-zA-Z0-9], so Arabic words fall back to the first word — use \p{L} as below. | code (js): function beats(tokens) {                                    // own sketch, Unicode-safe hero pick
  const n = Math.min(5, Math.max(3, Math.ceil(tokens.length / 6)));
  const parts = Array.from({ length: n }, (_, j) =>
    tokens.slice(Math.round(j * tokens.length / n), Math.round((j + 1) * tokens.length / n)));
  return parts.map((w) => { const core = (x) => x.replace(/[^\p{L}\p{N}]/gu, "");
    const h = Math.max(0, w.findIndex((x) => core(x).length >= 3 && core(x).length <= 10));
    return { lead: w.slice(0, h).join(" "), hero: w[h], tail: w.slice(h + 1).join(" ") }; });
}

Tween CSS custom properties that feed font-variation-settings (or @property) — no layout shift. Emphasis rule: jump weight 500 → 900 (150 ms crossfade) rather than scaling past 1.3×. Fonts on hand: Cairo[slnt,wght].ttf (200–1000, Latin + Arabic) and ReemKufi[wght].ttf in this skill's proofs/_shared/fonts; Arabic VFs also Noto Kufi/Naskh Arabic and Readex Pro. | optical settle (Fraunces) · opsz 144 → 72, wght 440 → 300, 0.45 s power2.out, local @font-face · hyperframes techniques ; emphasis without scale · wght 500 → 900, 150 ms; never >1.3× · kinetic-type playbook ; axis beat · wght or wdth 200 → 900 (Roboto Flex) · HF variable-axis-type ; per-character flex · weight + width hairline-condensed → black-wide, font-size eases inversely to hold the box, stagger 0.06 s · HF variable-font-flex ; weight wave · Recursive VF, crest wght 400 → 1000 travels the line, slnt −12, crestWidth 4, sweepSpeed 0.5, ltr or rtl, #f5f5f7 on #0b0b0d · HF weight-wave (canvas) ; width swell · wdth 62 → 125 with font-size until the word overflows, Archivo 900, 2–3 s power2.inOut · pm-pankajkumar-dev-0bee87 ; weight sweep + readout · wght 100 → 900, 0.6–0.8 s power2.inOut, mono caption shows the values · pm-tequilafunks-97f6c9 ; weight + tracking · wght 200 → 800 easeInOut 800 ms, letter-spacing 0.1em → 0, one letter accent · pm-sahildesigner23-ee3155 ; fast pops · wght 200 → 900 in 220 ms; 2 s major / 500 ms minor pulse · brief pm-zheke-38deff ; hero glyph stagger · 300 → 800, 30 ms per glyph, ≤12 glyphs · brief pm-itisrazak-3ad902 ; weight morph · wght 300 → 900 over 400 ms ease-out · pm-souravbhar871-61f424 | code (css): @font-face { font-family: CairoVF; src: url(Cairo[slnt,wght].ttf); font-weight: 200 1000; }
.hero { font-family: CairoVF; font-variation-settings: "wght" var(--w, 500); }
